      "text": "To determine the perimeter of triangle \\( XYZ \\), we start by identifying the coordinates of points \\( X \\), \\( Y \\), and \\( Z \\) in the right prism \\( ABCDEF \\) with height 16 and equilateral triangle bases of side length 12.\n\nFirst, we place the prism in a coordinate system for convenience:\n- \\( A = (0, 0, 0) \\)\n- \\( B = (12, 0, 0) \\)\n- \\( C = (6, -6, 0) \\)\n- \\( D = (6, -22, 0) \\)\n- \\( E = (0, 0, 16) \\)\n- \\( F = (12, 0, 16) \\)\n\nNext, we find the coordinates of the midpoints \\( X \\), \\( Y \\), and \\( Z \\):\n- \\( X \\) is the midpoint of \\( AC \\):\n\\[\nX = \\left( \\frac{0+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2}, \\frac{0+0}{2} \\right) = (3, -3, 0)\n\\]\n- \\( Y \\) is the midpoint of \\( BC \\):\n\\[\nY = \\left( \\frac{6+12}{2}, \\frac{-6+0}{2}, \\frac{0+0}{2} \\right) = (9, -3, 0)\n\\]\n- \\( Z \\) is the midpoint of \\( DC \\):\n\\[\nZ = \\left( \\frac{6+6}{2}, \\frac{-22-6}{2}, \\frac{0+0}{2} \\right) = (6, -14, 0)\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the distances between the points \\( X \\), \\( Y \\), and \\( Z \\) to find the sides of triangle \\( XYZ \\).\n\n1. Distance \\( XY \\):\n\\[\nXY = \\sqrt{(9-3)^2 + (-3+3)^2 + (0-0)^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 0^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{36} = 6\n\\]\n\n2. Distance \\( YZ \\):\n\\[\nYZ = \\sqrt{(6-9)^2 + (-14+3)^2 + (0-0)^2} = \\sqrt{(-3)^2 + (-11)^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 121} = \\sqrt{130}\n\\]\n\n3. Distance \\( ZX \\):\n\\[\nZX = \\sqrt{(3-6)^2 + (-3+14)^2 + (0-0)^2} = \\sqrt{(-3)^2 + 11^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 121} = \\sqrt{130}\n\\]\n\nThe perimeter of triangle \\( XYZ \\) is the sum of the lengths of its sides:\n\\[\nXY + YZ + ZX = 6 + \\sqrt{130} + \\sqrt{130} = 6 + 2\\sqrt{130}\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of triangle \\( XYZ \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6 + 2\\sqrt{130}}\n\\]",
