      "text": "To determine the perimeter of triangle \\( XYZ \\) in the given right prism, we need to find the coordinates of points \\( X \\), \\( Y \\), and \\( Z \\) and then calculate the perimeters of triangles \\( AXZ \\), \\( AYX \\), and \\( AZX \\).\n\nFirst, let's place the prism in a coordinate system. The base of the prism is an equilateral triangle with vertices \\( A(0,0) \\), \\( B(12,0) \\), and \\( C(6,-6) \\). The apex of the prism is at \\( E(0,-16) \\). Point \\( F \\) is directly above \\( E \\) at \\( F(12, -16) \\).\n\nNow, we find the coordinates of points \\( X \\), \\( Y \\), and \\( Z \\):\n- \\( X \\) is the midpoint of \\( AC \\). So, \\( X \\left( \\frac{0+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (3, -3) \\).\n- \\( Y \\) is the midpoint of \\( BC \\). So, \\( Y \\left( \\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (9, -3) \\).\n- \\( Z \\) is the midpoint of \\( DC \\). So, \\( Z \\left( \\frac{6+12}{2}, \\frac{-6-16}{2} \\right) = (9, -11) \\).\n\nNext, we calculate the lengths of the sides of triangle \\( XYZ \\):\n- The distance \\( XZ \\) is:\n  \\[\n  XZ = \\sqrt{(9-3)^2 + (-11+3)^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + (-8)^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 64} = \\sqrt{100} = 10.\n  \\]\n- The distance \\( XY \\) is:\n  \\[\n  XY = \\sqrt{(9-3)^2 + (-3+3)^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{36} = 6.\n  \\]\n- The distance \\( YZ \\) is:\n  \\[\n  YZ = \\sqrt{(9-9)^2 + (-3+11)^2} = \\sqrt{0^2 + 8^2} = \\sqrt{64} = 8.\n  \\]\n\nThe perimeter of triangle \\( XYZ \\) is the sum of these distances:\n\\[\nXY + YZ + XZ = 6 + 8 + 10 = 24.\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of triangle \\( XYZ \\) is \\(\\boxed{24}\\).",
